From: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fix callback signatures, return types and pointer mismatches

GCC 14 promotes -Wincompatible-pointer-types, -Wreturn-mismatch and
-Wint-conversion to errors, which surfaces sixteen long-standing type
errors in the demo sources. Each fix takes the type the surrounding
code already requires -- no behaviour is invented:

fm.c
  default_rds_cb() is assigned to a tAPP_FM_RDS_CBACK field
  (void (tBSA_FM_RDS_EVT, UINT8 *), fm.h:61) but took tBSA_FM_EVT.
  app_fm_rds_cback() is passed to BSA_FmRdsRegister() as a
  tBSA_FM_RDS_CBACK (bsa_fm_api.h:449, void (tBSA_FM_EVT, UINT8 *))
  but took UINT16. RDS event values are 2/8/14 so both are lossless.

fm_main.c
  app_fm_init() returns void; two callers tested "< 0" for failure.
  Dropped the dead test and kept the call.

test_vsc.c
  Three error paths in app_tm_vsc_tx_test()/app_tm_vsc_rx_test() did a
  bare "return;" from an int function documented "0 if success, -1
  otherwise". Return -1.

test_vse.c / test_vse.h
  app_tm_vse_pkt_count_callback() is a tAPP_TM_CUSTOM_CBACK
  (test_vse.h:67, BOOLEAN (tBSA_TM_EVT, tBSA_TM_MSG *)) and its body
  already ends in "return exit_cback;", but it was declared void.
  app_tm_vse_pkt_register() then handed that app-level callback
  straight to BSA instead of the void dispatcher; register
  app_tm_vse_generic_callback and stash the caller's callback in the
  control block, exactly as the sibling app_tm_vse_register() does.

app_ble_ancs.c
  notfn_thread is a tAPP_THREAD (pthread_t, an integer); cleared with
  NULL while the adjacent fields use 0. And a "return -1;" sat in
  ancs_client_send_next_get_notification_attributes_command(), whose
  own header block documents "Returns void".

app_ble_tvselect_server.c
  service_data_val is UINT8[BSA_DM_BLE_AD_UUID_MAX][BSA_DM_BLE_AD_DATA_LEN]
  (bsa_dm_api.h:322); the two assignments to a UINT8 * dropped the
  index that every neighbouring line uses.

pbapc.c (two identical copies in the tree)
  pbc_is_open() passes its BD_ADDR * to bdcpy(), which takes a BD_ADDR
  (bd.h:46). Dereference it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor demo tree, no upstream process]
Signed-off-by: Justin Schneck <j.schneck@peridio.com>
---
diff --git a/src/linux/app_ble_ancs/source/app_ble_ancs.c b/src/linux/app_ble_ancs/source/app_ble_ancs.c
index b4c016f..fad7422 100644
--- a/src/linux/app_ble_ancs/source/app_ble_ancs.c
+++ b/src/linux/app_ble_ancs/source/app_ble_ancs.c
@@ -359,7 +359,7 @@ int app_ble_ancs_register(void)
     ancs_clcb.thread_client_num = 0;
     ancs_clcb.thread_uid = 0;
     ancs_clcb.bNotfnThreadInitialized = FALSE;
-    ancs_clcb.notfn_thread = NULL;
+    ancs_clcb.notfn_thread = 0;
 
     return 0;
 }
@@ -488,7 +488,7 @@ void ancs_client_send_next_get_notification_attributes_command(UINT16 client_num
     if (status < 0)
     {
         APP_ERROR1("app_create_thread failed: %d", status);
-        return -1;
+        return;
     }
     else
         ancs_clcb.bNotfnThreadInitialized = TRUE;
